## 2. Another Major Thing

If you modify, fork, redistribute, repackage, or otherwise create a derivative version of this software, **you must change the name and branding of your version**.

In other words, **do not take your modified version and pretend that it is the original software.**

- You may say that your project is based on, derived from, or forked from this software.
- You may mention the original software and its author.
- You may keep copyright notices and license notices from the original software.
- You may absolutely make your own ridiculous derivative project.
- Just don't slap the original name and branding on your modified version and act like nothing happened.

But that applies only if you modify it and that's about it.

That's the one thing the author fucking cares about, and that does not count as a so-called "restriction".

